00:47:40,320 --> 00:47:41,240
All right.

185
00:47:41,240 --> 00:47:45,360
Well, before I throw something out, I'll try it.

186
00:47:45,360 --> 00:47:48,720
OK, so now the other way of value-driven games

187
00:47:48,720 --> 00:47:53,440
is what is called a moral form, also called a strategic form.

188
00:47:53,440 --> 00:47:59,200
Same concept, different word, different phrase.

189
00:47:59,200 --> 00:48:01,600
So what you do here is you display a complete grid

190
00:48:01,600 --> 00:48:04,400
of strategy profiles and payoffs.

191
00:48:04,400 --> 00:48:07,400
It's a complete grid of strategy profiles and payoffs.

192
00:48:07,400 --> 00:48:10,640
And the grid is one dimension per player.

193
00:48:10,640 --> 00:48:14,520
As you might guess, then, very often used for two-player games

194
00:48:14,520 --> 00:48:16,360
because it's really hard to go and draw

195
00:48:16,360 --> 00:48:19,600
three-dimensional grids.

196
00:48:19,600 --> 00:48:21,520
So if you just imagine what it would be like,

197
00:48:21,520 --> 00:48:23,080
so you'd have to actually be putting the payoffs

198
00:48:23,080 --> 00:48:24,120
in this three-dimensional grid.

199
00:48:24,120 --> 00:48:26,520
And then four-dimensional grids are really hard to draw.

200
00:48:26,520 --> 00:48:30,200
So when people do things like that,

201
00:48:30,200 --> 00:48:32,440
normally they'll just go and give you the equations,

202
00:48:32,440 --> 00:48:38,280
and they'll give up on actually trying to draw the grid.

203
00:48:38,280 --> 00:48:40,240
So the grid is one dimension per player.

204
00:48:40,240 --> 00:48:43,680
And the interesting thing about moral forms and moral forms

205
00:48:43,680 --> 00:48:46,800
is that they will often contain irrelevant information

206
00:48:46,800 --> 00:48:49,880
about what you would have done in situations that would never

207
00:48:49,880 --> 00:48:53,840
happen, even where you ended up, which is strange at first.

208
00:48:53,840 --> 00:48:57,640
But there is actually good reason for doing this.

209
00:48:57,640 --> 00:49:00,200
And as we're going to see, actually,

210
00:49:00,200 --> 00:49:02,840
your behavior in situations that don't occur

211
00:49:02,840 --> 00:49:04,800
can actually strategically change

212
00:49:04,800 --> 00:49:08,480
what happens in situations that do occur, which at first

