355
01:54:19,300 --> 01:54:21,260
He wants to get off too, so then you track him.

356
01:54:21,260 --> 01:54:22,620
So that one's not going to work.

357
01:54:22,620 --> 01:54:24,460
What if the criminal's on and Popeye's off?

358
01:54:24,460 --> 01:54:25,220
No, same reason.

359
01:54:25,220 --> 01:54:27,380
Then Popeye would want to get on too.

360
01:54:27,380 --> 01:54:29,460
What if they're both off?

361
01:54:29,460 --> 01:54:30,540
Is that going to work?

362
01:54:30,540 --> 01:54:32,500
No, because then the criminal wants to get on.

363
01:54:32,500 --> 01:54:36,060
And that's another case where we have no Nash equilibrium,

364
01:54:36,060 --> 01:54:37,180
which is also possible.

365
01:54:40,060 --> 01:54:42,020
So pure structure Nash equilibrium concept

366
01:54:42,020 --> 01:54:45,020
is the most used in all of economics and game theory,

367
01:54:45,020 --> 01:54:47,860
and probably all social science, actually.

368
01:54:47,860 --> 01:54:51,220
So it is used all the time, tons of papers.

369
01:54:51,220 --> 01:54:53,660
It's totally possible you guys will one day have a paper

370
01:54:53,660 --> 01:54:56,940
where you will use Nash equilibrium.

371
01:54:56,940 --> 01:54:59,460
It's a little bit odd, because it

372
01:54:59,460 --> 01:55:04,180
seems to assume away strategic interaction, which in a way

